    {
      "beat_id": "B01",
      "act": "RESOLVE + FETCH",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "estimated_duration_s": 24.0,
      "narration_text": "First, resolve the company. A ticker isn't the S E C's identifier, so the agent maps it to a C I K, the official company id. Then it fetches that company's structured X B R L data straight from EDGAR, the machine-readable version of the filing. It's cached, and it can run fully offline in sample mode.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "CARD",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeWindow",
          "props": {
            "view": "artifact",
            "artifactTitle": "Step 1-2: resolve, then fetch the filing",
            "artifactHeading": "ticker -> CIK -> official XBRL",
            "artifactLines": [
              "A ticker isn't the SEC's id -> map it to a CIK",
              "Fetch structured XBRL company facts from EDGAR",
              "Cached; runs fully offline in sample mode"
            ],
            "sparkLine": "Start from the official source."
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B01.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B01.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 20.84,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B01.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-09-28T16:12:05"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "act": "NORMALIZE",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "estimated_duration_s": 24.0,
      "narration_text": "Next, normalize. Companies tag the same concept differently, so the agent maps each metric it wants to an ordered list of known X B R L tags, records exactly which tag matched, and marks anything it can't find as missing. It never invents a number to fill a gap.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "CARD",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeWindow",
          "props": {
            "view": "artifact",
            "artifactTitle": "Step 3: normalize the concepts",
            "artifactHeading": "one metric, many possible tags",
            "artifactLines": [
              "Map each metric to an ordered list of us-gaap tags",
              "Record which tag actually matched",
              "Unmapped -> MISSING, never a guess"
            ],
            "sparkLine": "Map it; don't guess it."
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B02.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 17.62,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B02.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-09-28T16:12:05"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "DERIVE + VALIDATE",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "estimated_duration_s": 26.0,
      "narration_text": "Then it derives the ratios, margins, returns, and growth, keyed to the right reporting period. And it validates, each result comes back PASS, FAIL, or UNKNOWN, against checks like the accounting identity. Every value keeps a receipt, so you can trace any number back to its source tag.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "CARD",
